                                "sense_id": "ce5c5b67-8537-33bb-ae6e-d0e85325ed84",
                                "text": "1578, Raphael Holinshed et al., Chronicles of England, Scotlande, and Irelande, Volume I, Book 3, Chapter 1 “Of cattell kept for profit,” p. 222,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "354b9a4c-a888-4c18-ac77-cd8264cc6a36",
                                "sense_id": "ce5c5b67-8537-33bb-ae6e-d0e85325ed84",
                                "text": "And haue ye cattell too? and sheepe too?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8d3cf4e-6331-494f-b2a8-fe8e354bbd23",
                                "sense_id": "ce5c5b67-8537-33bb-ae6e-d0e85325ed84",
                                "text": "Or if a soule touch any vncleane thing, whether it be a carcase of an vncleane beast, or a carcase of vncleane cattell, or the carcase of vncleane creeping things, and if it be hidden from him, he also shall be vncleane, and guilty:"
                            }
                        ]
